{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1491493-a-hundred-room-101-s","id":1491493,"title":"A Hundred Room 101's","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-08-27T10:29:39-07:00","id":1491493,"title":"A Hundred Room 101's","content":"Related to the 'Sex and the Technocracy' thread, with the disappearance of control and the fracturing of Union leadership, I don't think there would be a unified Room 101 program. With leadership of each Construct falling to the Masters in charge of it, I think that Room 101 procedures and discipline would start to drift apart as the Technocrats go their various ways. So, you may have Constructs that severely punish things like Homophoia and Racism, and others that actively promote more colonial mindsets. Certainly, these Constructs would be a united front against various kinds of Reality Deviants, but the Ascension War is ultimately a Culture War, and differing Constructs will develop different cultures.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6358-robert-armsley","name":"Robert Armsley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6358_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-27T11:59:24-07:00","id":1491505,"title":"","content":"It would be interesting to consider an independent Room 101 Program in a Construct with few or no members of the NWO. The Netflix movie, <i><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=BfsNfFoA0J0\" target=\"_blank\">Spiderhead</a>,</i> could be a Progenitor version of Room 101.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":26467,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","user":"HorizonParty2021","date":". 08-27-2022, 03:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-27T16:15:16-07:00","id":1491525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1491493-a-hundred-room-101-s?p=1491505#post1491505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would be interesting to consider an independent Room 101 Program in a Construct with few or no members of the NWO. The Netflix movie, <i><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=BfsNfFoA0J0\" target=\"_blank\">Spiderhead</a>,</i> could be a Progenitor version of Room 101.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh wow, totally.<br /> <br /> Although I think the NWO would be entirely fine with Spiderhead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6358-robert-armsley","name":"Robert Armsley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6358_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-27T16:47:32-07:00","id":1491532,"title":"","content":"Room 101 is generally considered an NWO thing because what's really important is what is being done (adjusting the way people think), rather than how it is being done.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-28T10:58:34-07:00","id":1491623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Armsley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1491493-a-hundred-room-101-s#post1491493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Related to the 'Sex and the Technocracy' thread, with the disappearance of control and the fracturing of Union leadership, I don't think there would be a unified Room 101 program. With leadership of each Construct falling to the Masters in charge of it, I think that Room 101 procedures and discipline would start to drift apart as the Technocrats go their various ways. So, you may have Constructs that severely punish things like Homophoia and Racism, and others that actively promote more colonial mindsets. Certainly, these Constructs would be a united front against various kinds of Reality Deviants, but the Ascension War is ultimately a Culture War, and differing Constructs will develop different cultures.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>MtA, like VtM, WtA or any other WoD games, is set in the real world.<br /> <br /> It thus takes actual real world history, and place the games' stories on top of it, adjusting where necessary in order to have both syncronize.<br /> <br /> This means thus that, profound changes in the Meta will invariably cause the two worlds to fall out of sync given enough time.<br /> <br /> Yes, the lack of a central conditioning authority would invariably mean that each Amalgm will develop their own personal 101 rooms.<br /> <br /> This also means that the resulting world in the WoD would probably turn into a mess that would be very divergent from current affairs in the real world in a matter of a few decades - particularly considering how crazy the world's geopolitics are getting in just the last 3 years, and how unpredictable our future has become all of a sudden","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-07T14:32:32-07:00","id":1492557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Armsley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1491493-a-hundred-room-101-s#post1491493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Related to the 'Sex and the Technocracy' thread, with the disappearance of control and the fracturing of Union leadership, I don't think there would be a unified Room 101 program. With leadership of each Construct falling to the Masters in charge of it, I think that Room 101 procedures and discipline would start to drift apart as the Technocrats go their various ways. So, you may have Constructs that severely punish things like Homophoia and Racism, and others that actively promote more colonial mindsets. Certainly, these Constructs would be a united front against various kinds of Reality Deviants, but the Ascension War is ultimately a Culture War, and differing Constructs will develop different cultures.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking about the idea of bringing an awakened mage to a confined space to apply coercive pressure on them to change their bad, presumably <i>incorrect</i>, attitudes toward other people. Most mages have at least two of the nine spheres. The Awareness ability is important, since it governs auras and the chance to distinguish another mage from sleepers. A technocrat boss who wants to purge bad attitudes has the subject's own perceptual abilities to work with. The evidence that their attitude is misinformed is <i>out their in the world</i>. In most cases, correcting false beliefs about whole groups of people would involve sending the subject somewhere where the people in question are present with instructions that focus their attention on evidence disproving the attitudes.<br /> <br /> I made a post about mages' deeper perceptions: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1423165-effect-of-awakening-on-who-you-are-attracted-to\"><i>Effect of Awakening on who you're Attracted to</i></a>,<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1491493-a-hundred-room-101-s?p=1491623#post1491623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> MtA, like VtM, WtA or any other WoD games, is set in the real world.<br /> <br /> It thus takes actual real world history, and place the games' stories on top of it, adjusting where necessary in order to have both syncronize.<br /> <br /> This means thus that, profound changes in the Meta will invariably cause the two worlds to fall out of sync given enough time.<br /> <br /> Yes, the lack of a central conditioning authority would invariably mean that each Amalgm will develop their own personal 101 rooms.<br /> <br /> This also means that the resulting world in the WoD would probably turn into a mess that would be very divergent from current affairs in the real world in a matter of a few decades - particularly considering how crazy the world's geopolitics are getting in just the last 3 years, and how unpredictable our future has become all of a sudden</div> </div> </div> </div>The preparation a storyteller does is like writing a screenplay or novel. You don't actually create the whole world. You create those parts of the world that the characters can see and hear or otherwise sense that the plot focusses their attention on. The storytelling that's done after prep will require some improvisation. I think the game requires a bit of agreement from the outset to keep it playable. Any player can start with Correspondence 3 and decide to teleport to a part of the world the storyteller is unfamiliar with.<br /> <br /> Creating <i>one</i> original Room 101 in the local or regional setting does not seriously undermine the game's synchronicity with the real world. Having a hundred examples, including the original standard, to work with would be a good resource.<br /> <br /> One variation would be to make a Room 101 that is <i>very comfortable</i>, rather than <i>inescapable</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":26467,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","user":"HorizonParty2021","date":". 09-07-2022, 05:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-08T07:21:29-07:00","id":1492595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1491493-a-hundred-room-101-s?p=1492557#post1492557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One variation would be to make a Room 101 that is <i>very comfortable</i>, rather than <i>inescapable</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course! One of the terrifying things about the Union and Mages in general is that they often feel that they are working for the greater good. A Room 101 that love bombs someone and helps them become happy can make even the most hard core Traditionalist flip. But I propose that the further that a Room 101 conditions someone away from baseline cultural standards of behavior found in Sleeper society, the more energy needs to be put into keeping the subject 'mutual'.<br /> <br /> Depicting Mage as the horror game it should be, I can actually see a construct led by cultural conservatives doing something as heinous as Conversion Therapy for both queer or trans aspects of someone's personality, and it wouldn't be uncommon. This can drive an entire adventure as Tradition Mages who get wind of this place want to burn it to the ground (this presumes a Rogue Council era earthbound Construct.)<br /> <br /> And there would be a good number of Room 101's designed simply for torture.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6358-robert-armsley","name":"Robert Armsley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6358_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-08T17:23:37-07:00","id":1492645,"title":"","content":"Both the CIA and KGB did useless gay purges. The fear was that gay agents were vulnerable to blackmail by the enemy. The reality was that men who were forced to live in the closet by the culture of the time were so adapted to concealing an important aspect of their identity that they were often superior agents. <br /> <br /> Cultural Conservatism of the sort that would pursue conversion therapy is deeply emmeshed with Religious Fundamentalism. It isn't that the former c<i>an't</i> exist without the latter, but I think secular cultural conservatives committed to such practices would be rare. The Technocracy is not the Celestial Chorus. <br /> <br /> Appropriate backstory for a technocratic boss doing this sort of thing: He was a gay Chorus member who was blackmailed by the NWO into defecting to the Technocracy. Living on the straight and narrow and working to implement the timetable, his dreams are haunted by an incubus in tight jeans and assless chaps. He believes the incubus represents a subordinate who needs correction. It's actually his own Dynamic Avatar, calling him to shed the persona previously drilled into him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}